        "title": "Test Coverage Analysis",
        "content": "\n**Headline finding: there is no test suite anywhere in this repo.** No `*.test.ts`/`*.spec.ts` files, no jest/vitest in `web/package.json` (only `lint`/`typecheck` scripts exist). `engine/pyproject.toml` lists `pytest` as a dev dependency but there's no `tests/` directory and no `[tool.pytest]` config — it's declared, unused. Coverage is 0%.\n\n**Second finding that changes how to read this report:** `engine/` is almost entirely unimplemented. Every pipeline/agent/eval function body is `raise NotImplementedError(\"Phase N — see AGENTS.md § ...\")` per the phased build order in AGENTS.md. So for most of `engine/`, this isn't \"missing tests for existing code\" — it's pre-implementation. I've separated those into **TDD skeletons** (write these *before* implementing, since AGENTS.md already specifies the exact contract) rather than treating them as coverage debt.\n\n`web/` is the opposite: substantially implemented (sources, rulesets, runs, export, audit, engine-proxy routes all have real logic) and **completely untested**. That's where the real coverage gaps are.\n\nOne more gap worth flagging up front: **the conflict review routes don't exist yet** (`app/api/conflicts/route.ts`, `app/api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution/route.ts` — documented in AGENTS.md, absent from the tree). That's the core human-review workflow (approve/reject/override + audit). Not a coverage gap today, but the highest-priority integration surface once built.\n\n---\n\n",
