      {
        "title": "engine/pyproject.toml — add",
        "content": "[tool.pytest.ini_options]\ntestpaths = [\"tests\"]\n```\n```\nengine/tests/\n  pipeline/test_schema.py\n  pipeline/test_normalize.py\n  pipeline/test_blocking.py\n  pipeline/test_detect.py\n  agent/test_graph.py\n  agent/test_prompts.py\n  eval/test_generate.py\n  eval/test_baselines.py\n  eval/test_harness.py\n  test_main.py          # FastAPI TestClient\n  test_db.py            # needs a test Postgres or mocking — see §5\n```\n\n**TypeScript** — no framework installed. Per AGENTS.md's \"ask before installing\" rule: **I'd recommend Vitest** (ESM-native, fast, works cleanly with Next.js App Router route handlers and Zod schemas without a DOM by default; add `@testing-library/react` + `jsdom` only if/when component tests are wanted). This needs your go-ahead before I add it to `package.json`.\n\n---\n\n",
